Bacteria specs fail under parallel Jest load; Jest workers do not exit gracefully
status:create-spec
Found while checking PR #3147 (#3103 step 3b) locally.

In `nx run-many -t test` over the bacteria projects:
- libs/features/bacteria-engine/src/lib/state/replay/replay-pack.spec.ts failed once (the suite took 42.8 s);
- in another run, libs/features/lazy/bacteria-game/src/lib/storage/local-game-replays.spec.ts failed once.

Both pass alone, repeatedly, with and without the PR's change, so they look timing-sensitive under load (likely a timeout). Jest also reports a worker that fails to exit gracefully in the game lib and in the engine (leaking timers).

Why it matters: on the shared Nx Cloud workers this could make CI flaky.

Related: #3103 (where it was found), #3120 (another bacteria CI flake, e2e wait-for-webserver).
